{
  "name": "_shootingPracticeSetupMenu",
  "comment": "OpenSWOS's SHOOTING PRACTICE setup screen, from the PRACTICE submenu's SHOOTING PRACTICE button (shooting_practice.c ShootingPracticeMenu). The choices before the drill: DEFENDERS OFF/ON (ON keeps the computer's RB, LB and D players on the pitch) and MIDFIELD OFF/ON (ON keeps its M, LW and RW too); attackers are always stripped. Each row draws through its string table (_practiceDefendersStrTable / _practiceMidfieldStrTable, indexed by its flag) and is recoloured green/yellow by ShootingPracticeSetupInit (onInit AND onReturn, since every ShowMenu re-unpacks the baked colour) and ChangePracticeDefenders / ChangePracticeMidfield. CONTINUE (ShootingPracticeContinue) runs the friendly flow with the mode flag set; it must not call CommonMenuExit (docs/MENUS.md section 12). Both targets: a classic packed menu, so the m68k build gets it from the baked src/menu_data.c. ATTACK UP/DOWN selects the human attacking direction for the whole untimed session; Escape ends practice.",
